title: Evilginx2 Adversary-in-the-Middle Phishing Against M365
id: c0cf7e0a-9168-42e3-b017-328e1aee0812
status: experimental
description: Detects Evilginx2-based adversary-in-the-middle phishing sessions targeting Microsoft 365. The BigBear 2.0 PhaaS platform proxies the real Microsoft login flow, intercepts session cookies post-authentication, and injects JavaScript to disable FIDO2/WebAuthn on phishing pages. Uses residential proxy pools across 69 countries.
references:
  - https://cyber.netsecops.io/articles/bigbear-2-0-phishing-service-bypasses-mfa-in-global-m365-campaign/
  - https://www.cloudsek.com
  - https://www.bleepingcomputer.com
author: Tia N. List
date: 2026-09-10
tags:
  - attack.t1557
  - attack.t1566
logsource:
  category: network_connection
  product: windows
detection:
  selection_m365_auth:
    dst_host|contains: 'login.microsoftonline.com'
  filter_loopback:
    src_ip: '127.0.0.1'
  selection_fido2_disable:
    dst_host|contains: 'login.microsoftonline.com'
    http_user_agent|contains: 'Evilginx'
  selection_session_anomaly:
    dst_host|contains: 'login.microsoftonline.com'
    http_request_uri|contains: 'oauth2/authorize'
    http_request_uri|contains: 'response_mode'
  condition: selection_m365_auth and selection_session_anomaly and not filter_loopback
falsepositives:
  - Legitimate M365 authentication from unusual IPs
  - Cloud proxy services
level: high
